<title>MEXICO: Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate falls in auction.</title>
<headline>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate falls in auction.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate fell in this week's primary auction and demand rose, Banco de Mexico said.</p>
<p>Auction results were: (all rates in percent)</p>
<p>Maturity    Weighted Avg   Change (bps)  Min Rate  Max Rate</p>
<p>28-Day	20.23	    -238	    20.23     20.24</p>
<p>91-Day	21.93	    -104	    21.89     21.98</p>
<p>182-Day     22.46	     -53	    22.34     22.49</p>
<p>343-Day     23.72				23.59     23.80</p>
<p>Last week the 350-day paper was assigned at 24.29 pct.  </p>
<p>Maturity    Assigned	  Demand		Bid/Cover</p>
<p>28-Day	800 million pesos   5.79 bln pesos    7.24</p>
<p>91-Day	800 million pesos   6.66 bln pesos    8.33</p>
<p>182-Day     800 million pesos   3.77 bln pesos    4.71</p>
<p>343-Day     600 million pesos   2.80 bln pesos    4.66</p>
<p>The bid-to-cover ratio for the auction as a whole was 6.34 on demand of 19.02 billion pesos compared with 5.47 the week before, on demand of 16.40 billion pesos the week before. Tails were as follows:</p>
<p>    28-Day			    1 basis point</p>
<p>    91-Day			    5 basis points</p>
<p>    182-Day			   3 basis points</p>
<p>    343-Day			   8 basis points</p>
<p>((--Dan Trotta, Mexico City newsroom, +525 728-9559))</p>
